      "properties": {
        "cnr_id": "ComfyUI-Pixaroma",
        "ver": "1227d9898f9d5137533df750611ca97e8c738f3d",
        "Node name for S&R": "PixaromaNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "{\"version\": 1, \"content\": \"<h1>MiniMax H3 - Low VRAM (8 GB)</h1><p>Tested on an 8 GB card. The 20 GB video model and the 15 GB text encoder are streamed from system RAM, so you need about <strong>32 GB of system RAM</strong> as well as the 8 GB of VRAM.</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\"><h2>Measured run times on 8 GB</h2><ul><li>352 x 608, 3 sec - 30 seconds</li><li>416 x 736, 5 sec - 55 seconds</li><li>480 x 864, 5 sec - 80 seconds</li><li>480 x 864, 8 sec - 130 seconds</li></ul><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\"><h2>Why the sizes stop at 480 x 864</h2><p>The cost is size and length multiplied together, not either one alone. Everything up to about 118,000 blocks finished on 8 GB; 141,000 failed. The list here plus the 8 second maximum tops out at 92,340 blocks, which leaves real headroom.</p><p>blocks = latent frames x (height / 16) x (width / 16)</p><p>If you have more VRAM you can add bigger sizes with the gear on the Sizes node, but raise the size or the seconds, not both.</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\"><h2>Do not delete the two Free VRAM nodes</h2><p>They unload the previous model before the next one loads. Without them the H3 VAE gets split between the graphics card and the computer, and the run stops with a device mismatch error. This bites the SMALL sizes hardest, so a quick test without them looks fine and then fails later.</p><p>They come from the ComfyUI LayerStyle pack. If they show up red, install it from the ComfyUI Manager.</p>\"}",
        ""
      ],
      "color": "#1d1d1d",
      "bgcolor": "#2a2a2a"
    },
